/* Reuses parts of the :: Moor Abduction event */
:: Fishing Moor Hiker Attack
<<effects>>
<<set $fishingMoorHikersCount to 1>>
<<if $rng gte 70>>
	<<set $fishingMoorHikersCount to 2>>
<</if>>

You're watching your line when you hear movement in the heather behind you. <span class="red"><<if $fishingMoorHikersCount is 1>>Someone grabs you from behind and slams you to the ground<<else>>Multiple hands are on you before you can turn, dragging you to the ground<</if>></span>.
<br><br>

<<link [[Fight|Fishing Moor Hiker Molestation]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Molestation
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<generate1>>
	<<if $fishingMoorHikersCount is 2>>
		<<generate2>>
	<</if>>
	<<unset $fishingMoorHikersCount>>
	<<maninit>>
	<<hawkRescueSetup>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<man>>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>

<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Hiker Molestation Finish]]>><</link>></span>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Hiker Molestation]]>><</link>></span>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Molestation Finish
<<effects>>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<ejaculation>>
	<<if $rng gte 70>>
		The <<if $enemyno gt 1>><<group>><<else>><<person>><</if>> laugh<<if $enemyno is 1>>s<</if>> roughly as <<if $enemyno gt 1>>they<<else>><<he>><</if>> finish<<if $enemyno is 1>>es<</if>> with you. "Remy will want this one," <<person1>><<if $enemyno is 1>><<person>> says<<else>><<person>> says, and <<his>> companion nods<</if>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if !pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			Rough hands force your wrists behind you, and bind them together.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<tearful>>, you're pulled to your feet and marched across the moor, your rod left behind. <<handheldruined>>
		<br><br>

		<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>
		<<clotheson>>
		<<endcombat>>
		<<bind>>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

		<<link [[Next|Moor Abduction]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		The <<if $enemyno gt 1>><<group>> laugh<<else>><<person>> laughs<</if>> roughly, seemingly satisfied. "That was easy," <<if $enemyno gt 1>>one of them says<<else>><<he>> says<</if>>.
		<br><br>

		<<tearful>> you scramble to gather yourself as <<if $enemyno gt 1>>they wander<<else>><<he>> wanders<</if>> off into the moor, disappearing into the heather.
		<br><br>

		<<clotheson>>
		<<endcombat>>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

		<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $alarm is 1 and $rescue is 1>>
	The <<if $enemyno gt 1>><<group>> begin<<else>><<person>> begins<</if>> to curse as a <<hawkScreechDesc>> pierces the air. <<hawkRescueApproachSentence>>
	<br><br>

	The <<if $enemyno gt 1>><<group>>, panicked, scatter<<else>><<person>>, panicked, flees<</if>> in different directions, disappearing into the moor.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	<<npc "Great Hawk">><<person1>>
	<<tearful>> you search the heavens for <<if $syndromebird is 1>>your <<if $monster is 1>><<nnpc_wife "Great Hawk">><<else>>partner<</if>><<else>>whatever your assailant saw<</if>>. You quickly find what you're looking for, seeing <<if $syndromebird is 1>>your<<else>>a<</if>> <<beasttype>> flying towards you as fast as <<bhis>> wings can carry <<bhim>>.
	<br><br>

	<<if $syndromebird is 1>>
		<<link [[Next|Bird Rescue Syndrome]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Next|Bird Rescue No Syndrome]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	<<if $enemyno gt 1>>
		You manage to land enough strikes between them to drive them back. They exchange a look and scatter into the heather without another word.
		<br><br>

		<<tearful>> you catch your breath, watching the heather settle.
		<br><br>

		<<clotheson>>
		<<endcombat>>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

		<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		You land a solid strike against the <<person1>><<person>>. <<He>> staggers back, and you hold your ground, watching until <<he>> retreats into the heather.
		<br><br>

		<<tearful>> you catch your breath, watching the heather settle.
		<br><br>

		<<clotheson>>
		<<endcombat>>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

		<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Leave|Moor]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Arrive
<<effects>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "sit">>
<<run fishingRecordNpcArrivalTime()>>
<<generate1>>
<<generate2>>
<<saveNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">>
<<saveNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">>

Two figures crest over a low hill nearby, heading toward you. One of them raises a hand when they spot you. They look like hikers.
<br><br>

<<if $exposed gte 1>>
	"Didn't think there'd be anyone else out here, especially someone so..." <<he>> glances at your <<lewdness>> "...adventurous," the <<person1>><<person>> says as they draw near. <<fameexhibitionism 2>>
<<else>>
	"Didn't think there'd be anyone else out here," the <<person1>><<person>> says as they draw near, glancing at your rod.
<</if>>
<<His>> companion, a <<person2>><<person>> sets down a bag with a quiet clink. "We're looking to sit down and take a little break, mind if we set up nearby? We won't crowd you."
<br><br>

<<link [[Sure|Fishing Moor Hiker Sit]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Wave them off|Fishing Moor Wait]]>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>
	<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
	<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
	<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
	<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>
	<<endevent>>
<</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Sit
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.spike to dangerEvent(0.35)>>

They settle down a short distance off to the side. The <<person2>><<person>> produces a pair of cans from <<his>> bag and pops one open, passing the other to <<his>> companion.
<<if $exposed gte 1>>
	<<He>> catches <<his>> companion's eye as <<he>> hands the can over, both of them glancing at your <<lewdness>> before looking back at each other. They clink their cans, one of them chuckling quietly.
<<else>>
	They clink them together quietly.<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<</if>>

<<if $exposed gte 1>>
	<<fameexhibitionism 3>>
	<<exhibitionism1>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Leave
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>

The <<person1>><<person>> stretches and nudges the other. "Better head back," <<he>> says. They start gathering their things, and before too long they're heading across the moor, giving you a brief wave before they go.
<br><br>

<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Leave Weather
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>

The <<person1>><<person>> squints into the rain. "Right, we're off." They start gathering their things. "Don't stay out too long, it's not safe in these parts."
<br><br>

<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Leave Dusk
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>

The <<person1>><<person>> gets to <<his>> feet, brushing heather from <<his>> clothes. "We're losing the light," <<he>> says with a glance towards the sky. <<His>> companion nods and starts packing up. They wave farewell and head off into the dusk.
<br><br>

<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Leave Night
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>

<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase is "campfire">>
	The <<person1>><<person>> pokes at the dying embers and looks up at the dark sky. "It's getting late, we should head out."
<<else>>
	The <<person1>><<person>> looks up at the dark sky. "It's getting late, we should head out."
<</if>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>

The pair bid you farewell and pick their way off into the dark.
<br><br>

<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Hikers Drink Offer On PC Leave
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>

<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase is "sit" and $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkCount gte 1 and ($daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.spike or $rng gte 70)>>
	The <<person1>><<person>> glances at the can. "You should finish that off before you go. We'll take the empty back with us."
	<br><br>

	<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.spike>>
		<<silently>><<englishdifficulty 500 1200>><</silently>>
		<<if $englishSuccess>>
			There's something a little too eager in the way they watch you, it's as if this matters more to them than it should.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.spike>>
		<<link [[Finish the drink|Fishing Moor Spiked Drink Leave]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Finish the drink|Fishing Moor Hiker Drink Leave Chug]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Decline and Leave|Moor]]>>
		<<endevent>>
		<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>
		<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
		<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
		<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>
		<<set $eventskip to 1>>
	<</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase is "campfire">>
		The <<person1>><<person>> gives you a warm smile as you pack up. "Take care out there, and thanks again for the meal."<<llstress>><<stress -10>>
	<<else>>
		The <<person2>><<person>> smiles as you pack up. "Take care out there," <<he>> says with a small wave. "Be safe."<<lstress>><<stress -5>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>
	<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
	<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
	<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
	<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

	<<link [[Next|Moor]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Hiker Drink Leave Chug
<<effects>>
<<alcohol `($daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkCount * 10)`>><<ggalcohol>>

You tip the can back and drain the rest in a few long swallows. The hikers cheer, grinning as you hand the empty can over.
<br><br>

"Cheers" the <<person1>><<person>> says, crushing the can before tucking it away. "Safe travels."<<lstress>><<stress -4>>
<br><br>

<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.eventDanger to 0>>
<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>

<<link [[Next|Moor]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Spiked Drink Leave
<<drugs 180>>
<<effects>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkCount to 0>>

You tip the can back and drain the rest before handing it over, and the <<person2>><<person>> takes it from you with a pleased little smile.
<br><br>

You turn away, and before you get ten steps away, you begin to feel dizzy. You blink. The moor looks further away than it should, and the sound of the water is oddly distant. Your legs feel unreliable beneath you. Why is the ground moving towards you?
<br><br>

<<link [[...|Fishing Moor Spiked Drink 2]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>


:: Fishing Moor Campfire Cook
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.spike to false>>

The <<person2>><<person>> stands and begins gathering sticks while the other clears a small patch of ground. Within a few minutes they have a fire going, the fish propped on a flat stone above the flames. The smell of it drifts around the three of you.
<br><br>

<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkCount lte 0 and !$daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkOffered and !(playerIsPregnant() and playerAwareTheyArePregnant())>>
	<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkOffered to true>>
	While the fish cooks, the <<person1>><<person>> produces a pair of cans from the bag. "May as well," <<he>> says, and offers you one.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Accept|Fishing Moor Campfire Eat]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.drinkCount to 10>><<pass 15>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Decline|Fishing Moor Campfire Eat]]>><<endevent>><<pass 15>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Campfire Eat]]>><<endevent>><<pass 15>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Campfire Eat
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "campfire">>

After a couple minutes, the $fishingHookedFish.type is ready to eat, skin blackened on the side where it was resting against the rock. The hikers break it apart with their hands, the <<person2>><<person>> passing you a good hunk of the meat.
<br><br>

You sit in a loose ring around the fire, eating in comfortable silence. The <<person1>><<person>> licks <<his>> fingers and leans back. "Not bad for something caught out here," <<he>> says. You almost feel like the fire is pushing back the evils of the world. <<stress -20>><<lllstress>>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


