<</if>>


:: Fishing Moor Cat Eat Hikers
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
You open wide and drop the whole $fishingHookedFish.type in your mouth. <<fishingEatFishTfProgress>><<lstress>><<stress -6>>
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

Both the hikers go quiet, staring at you with a confused look on their faces.
<<if $rng gte 80>>
	Without a word, they start packing up their things, giving you looks that are a mix of concern and confusion as they leave.
	<<set $fishing.fishingMoor.event to "none">>
	<<set $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase to "finished">>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $daily.fishing.fishingMoor.hikers.phase is "finished">>
	<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_1">>
	<<clearNPC "moor_hiker_2">>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Wait]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Fishing Moor Hiker Exposed Attack
<<effects>>
<<loadNPC 0 "moor_hiker_1">><<person1>>
<<loadNPC 1 "moor_hiker_2">><<person2>>
The <<person1>><<person>> sets down <<his>> can and stands up slowly. <<He>> looks you over, and the <<person2>><<person>> follows <<his>> gaze before getting to <<his>> feet as well. "Just standing around like that is an invitation," <<he>> says, eying your <<lewdness>>. "And I think we're happy to take you up on it."<<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Moor Hiker Exposed Molestation]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>


